# Trivy security policy exceptions with justifications
#
# AWS-0132 / AVD-AWS-0132 (S3 Bucket Default Encryption — KMS CMK not used):
# Resource: infrastructure/terraform/bootstrap/s3.tf (aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration.terraform_state)
# Suppression: Inline annotation only — see #trivy:ignore:AVD-AWS-0132 on s3.tf line 19.
# Global suppression intentionally removed. The inline annotation provides narrowly-scoped,
# resource-level suppression. No global override is present in this file.
#
# Justification: S3 bootstrap bucket uses AWS-managed AES256 server-side encryption to prevent
# circular dependencies during initial remote state backend bootstrapping prior to KMS provisioning.
# State data is protected via defense-in-depth controls:
# 1. Strict TLS/HTTPS transport enforcement via bucket policy (DenyInsecureTransport / aws:SecureTransport: false).
# 2. Complete public access block (block_public_acls, block_public_policy, ignore_public_acls, restrict_public_buckets).
# 3. Object versioning enabled to prevent accidental state deletion or corruption.
# 4. Lifecycle rule expiring noncurrent state versions after 30 days.
